Suppose that, for every strictly positive probability vector $\lambda$ on $E$, there is a random normalized gradient $F\in V$ such that $$\label{eq:weighted-target}
 \|F\|_\infty\le K\quad\text{almost surely},\qquad
 \sum_{e\in E}\lambda_e\left|\mathbb E|F_e|^p-b\right|\le\eta b.$$ The numbers $b$ and $K$ are the same for all $\lambda$.

outputs.exact_statement:
Fix $1<p<\infty$, $p\ne2$, and put $$\gamma(p)=
 \begin{cases}
  2-p,&1<p<2,\\
  1-2/p,&2<p<\infty.
 \end{cases}$$ For every $D>1$ there is a constant $C_{p,D}<\infty$ such that, for every integer $n\ge2$, $$\label{eq:main-bounds}
 \frac{\log n}{\log(1+2D)}
 \le d_p(n,D)
 \le \exp\!\bigl(C_{p,D}(\log n)^{\gamma(p)}\bigr).$$ For exact embeddings, $$\label{eq:exact-bounds}
 \left\lfloor\frac{n-1}{4}\right\rfloor^2
 \le d_p(n,1)\le\binom n2\qquad(n\ge9).$$ Consequently, $$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{\log d_p(n,D)}{\log n}
 =\begin{cases}0,&D>1,\\2,&D=1.\end{cases}$$

Let $0<\eta<1/3$ and $b,K\ge1$. Suppose that, for every strictly positive probability vector $\lambda$ on $E$, there is a random normalized gradient $F\in V$ such that $$\label{eq:weighted-target}
 \|F\|_\infty\le K\quad\text{almost surely},\qquad
 \sum_{e\in E}\lambda_e\left|\mathbb E|F_e|^p-b\right|\le\eta b.$$ The numbers $b$ and $K$ are the same for all $\lambda$. Then the points admit an embedding into $\ell_p^d$ with distortion at most $$\left(\frac{1+3\eta}{1-3\eta}\right)^{1/p},$$ where $$\label{eq:sampling-dimension}
 d\le\left\lceil
 C\max\left\{1,\frac{K^{2p}}{\eta^2b^2}\right\}\log(2n)
 \right\rceil$$ for an absolute constant $C$.

Let $h$ be a bounded real function supported on a region of finite $\nu$-measure, and let $S$ be its signed Poisson sum. Then $$\begin{aligned}
 \mathbb Ee^{itS}
 &=\exp\left(\int(\cos(th)-1)\,d\nu\right),\label{eq:poisson-cf}\\
 \mathbb Ee^{tS}
 &=\exp\left(\int(\cosh(th)-1)\,d\nu\right),\label{eq:poisson-mgf}\\
 \mathbb ES&=0,\qquad \mathbb ES^2=\int h^2\,d\nu.\label{eq:poisson-variance}
\end{aligned}$$ The characteristic-function identity also holds for unbounded $h$ on a finite-measure region.

There exist a unit vector $w=(w_1,\ldots,w_N)\in W^N$ and an $r$-dimensional subspace $U\subset w^\perp\subset H^N$ with the following properties.*


1.  *The vectors $w_1,\ldots,w_N$ span $W$, and $$\label{eq:inverse-pairings}
     \sum_{i=1}^N w_i^T Cw_i\ne0
     \qquad\text{whenever }[C]\in\mathcal C.$$*


2.  *The map $$\label{eq:projection-U}
     P_W^N\big|_U:U\longrightarrow w^\perp\cap W^N$$ is an isomorphism.*


3.  *Suppose that $F_\infty,F_0\subset H$ are orthogonal subspaces, $C_0$ is a symmetric operator on $F_0$, and $\dim(F_\infty\oplus F_0)>d_*$. No nonzero tuple $u=(u_1,\ldots,u_N)\in U$ satisfies $$\label{eq:forbidden-projections}
     P_{F_\infty}u_i=0,\qquad
     P_{F_0}u_i=C_0P_{F_0}w_i
     \qquad(1\le i\le N).$$

There exist a linear functional $\Lambda:\mathbb R[s_1,\ldots,s_7]_{\le4}\to\mathbb R$ and an open ball $\Omega\subset\Omega_0$ about zero with the following properties:*

1.  *$\Lambda(1)=1$, and its moment matrix on polynomials of degree at most two is positive definite;*




2.  *for every $c\in\Omega$, writing $$\label{eq:tested-patch}
      (A_{c,\varepsilon},t_{c,\varepsilon},y_{c,\varepsilon})
      =\Lambda_s\bigl(x(c+\varepsilon s)\bigr),$$ there are constants $a_c>0$ and $\kappa_c>0$ such that, as $\varepsilon\downarrow0$, $$\begin{gathered}
      \label{eq:deformation-lower-bound}
      A_{c,\varepsilon}\succeq a_c\varepsilon^4 I_r,\\
      \label{eq:deformation-violation}
      t_{c,\varepsilon}-\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}\bigl(A_{c,\varepsilon}^{-1}Q(y_{c,\varepsilon})\bigr)
      =-\kappa_c\varepsilon^4+o(\varepsilon^4).

    \end{gathered}$$ All three entries of <a href="#eq:tested-patch" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:tested-patch">[eq:tested-patch]</a> remain bounded as $\varepsilon\downarrow0$.
